  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;LONGTOWN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Longtown is a census-designated place (CDP) and unincorporated community in Pittsburg County, Oklahoma, United States, with historical and geographical details."&lt;SEP&gt;"Longtown is a location in Pittsburg County, Oklahoma, USA, known for its sheep market and population growth over the years."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0306-29081c64f3b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOBUCKSY COUNTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tobucksy County is a county in the Indian Territory where Longtown was originally located."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tobucksy County is a historical county in the Choctaw Nation, Indian Territory, where Longtown was originally located."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0306-29081c64f3b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHOCTAW NATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Choctaw Nation is a Native American tribal nation, historically located in the southeastern United States, including parts of Oklahoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0306-29081c64f3b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDIAN TERRITORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indian Territory was a region in the United States where Native American tribes were relocated, including parts of modern-day Oklahoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0306-29081c64f3b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GAINES COUNTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gaines County is a historical county that bordered Tobucksy County, as indicated by the boundary of Longtown Creek."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0306-29081c64f3b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PITTSBURG, OKLAHOMA, USA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pittsburg, Oklahoma, USA is the current location of Longtown, as it has moved from its original location in the Indian Territory."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0306-29081c64f3b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONGTOWN SHEEP MARKET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Longtown Sheep Market is a significant event in Longtown's history, facilitating the spread of an infectious disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0306-29081c64f3b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WILLIAM HOWARD SCHOOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"William Howard School is a secondary school located in Brampton, which many Longtown students travel to."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0306-29081c64f3b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARLISLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carlisle is a city where many Longtown students travel for secondary education, and it is also the location of a rejected planning application."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0306-29081c64f3b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCHINVAR SCHOOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lochinvar School was a secondary school in Longtown until 2008, after which students began traveling to Carlisle for secondary education."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0306-29081c64f3b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARLISLE CITY COUNCIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carlisle City Council is the governing body that rejected a planning application for a water storage facility in 2014."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0306-29081c64f3b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2000 CENSUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 2000 census is a significant event that provides population data for Longtown."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0306-29081c64f3b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;U.S. CENSUS BUREAU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The U.S. Census Bureau is the organization responsible for conducting the census and providing population statistics."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0306-29081c64f3b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POPULATION DEVELOPMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Population development refers to the changes in population over time, as seen in the census data."</data>
